    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 923,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Pothinus\nPothinus or Potheinos ( early 1st century BC to 48 or 47 BC ) , a eunuch , was regent for Pharaoh Ptolemy XIII of the Ptolemaic dynasty of Ancient Egypt . He is most remembered for turning Ptolemy against his sister and co-ruler Cleopatra VII , thus starting a civil war , and for having Pompey decapitated and presenting the severed head to Julius Caesar . When Ptolemy XII died in 51 BC his will stated that Ptolemy XIII and Cleopatra VII were to become co-rulers of Egypt , with the Roman Republic as their guardians . Ptolemy XIII was underage and Pothinus was appointed as his regent . The general Achillas and the rhetorician Theodotus of Chios were also guardians of the Egyptian king . When Ptolemy and Cleopatra were elevated to the status of senior rulers , Pothinus was maintained as the former 's regent . Most Egyptologists believed that Pothinus used his influence to turn Ptolemy against Cleopatra ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
